      <title>Manchester United v Tottenham: Premier League – live</title>
      <link>https://www.theguardian.com/football/live/2026/oct/10/manchester-united-v-tottenham-premier-league-live</link>
      <description>&lt;p&gt;⚽ Updates from the 5.30pm BST kick-off at Old Trafford&lt;br&gt;⚽ &lt;a href="https://www.theguardian.com/football/live"&gt;Scores&lt;/a&gt; | &lt;a href="https://www.theguardian.com/football/premierleague/table"&gt;Table&lt;/a&gt; | &lt;a href="mailto:scott.murray@theguardian.com"&gt;Mail Scott&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Spurs get the ball rolling.&lt;/strong&gt; They’re kicking towards the Stretford End in this first half.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The teams are out.&lt;/strong&gt; Manchester United in their famous red, white and black, Tottenham in second-choice dark blue with diagonal multi-coloured neon nonsense. Meanwhile here’s the first line of a song ringing out &lt;em&gt;loud&lt;/em&gt; from all four corners of Old Trafford: “You know what you are.” No prizes for guessing the rest of the lyrics, or which club they’re serenading. Don’t look back in anger? Good luck with that! We’ll be off in a minute.&lt;/p&gt; &lt;a href="https://www.theguardian.com/football/live/2026/oct/10/manchester-united-v-tottenham-premier-league-live"&gt;Continue reading...&lt;/a&gt;</description>
