      <title>Ipswich’s O’Shea and Ouattara stun Fulham with last-gasp comeback win</title>
      <link>https://www.theguardian.com/football/2026/oct/10/ipswich-fulham-premier-league-match-report</link>
      <description>&lt;p&gt;Ipswich produced a dramatic turnaround to beat Fulham 2-1 after late goals by Abdoul Ouattara and Dara O’Shea extended Álvaro Arbeloa’s winless start to six Premier League matches.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The former Real Madrid manager had been on course to toast a maiden league victory in charge of the Cottagers after Ryan Sessegnon’s sweet 55th-minute strike put the visitors ahead. It would have eased the pressure on Arbeloa, but the Spaniard watched his team collapse, with Ouattara producing a spectacular 30-yard equaliser with two minutes left before O’Shea, the Ipswich captain, headed home in stoppage time to spark wild celebrations at Portman Road.&lt;/p&gt; &lt;a href="https://www.theguardian.com/football/2026/oct/10/ipswich-fulham-premier-league-match-report"&gt;Continue reading...&lt;/a&gt;</description>
